From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] Record when each GPU client's frames reached the screen

To decide whether games belong on the Mihawk desktop, the same game must be
measured in both presentation routes. The broker replies to a present only
after the display flip in both: the launcher flips the client's own buffer
(direct), the desktop copies the completed frame and composes the scene on
the CPU (composed). Each client now keeps a frame pacing record
(src/pw_frame_pacing.h): intervals between shown presents' ends in 250 us
buckets, stalls over 20 and 34 ms, presents another process's screen hid,
and the time inside its shown presents. A line goes to the record and to
stderr every 10 s of activity and when the client closes.

Base: PS5_Vulkan 87a48676dda0977d5ba8ff1ddcf02816d41c443b + 0001-0004
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
